The tester's real-phone round (box 54550, 12 Oct):

(1) Goal 24996: after the accountant request the owner typed „ლიკას კითხე",
and the helper received exactly „ლიკას კითხე" as the whole question. The
model's ask was refused (wrong goal), it opened a goal and proposed a plan;
the plan refusal sent the instruction itself (§97 path), and with no
question and no need in the line the question fell back to the whole
sentence. Now such a line sends nothing and opens no goal: the refusal
tells the run to ask, and the run read the earlier message.

(3) Goal 24989: „იცნობ ზაზა გამოგონილს…?" — „ზაზა" was read as the trade
and the helper got a picker of her own contacts called Zaza under a yes/no
question. A Georgian first name (the base's own list, the ambiguous ones
excepted) is a person, not a need; no picker.

